      "writtenOn": "2025-05-11T16:35:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first I wondered if we could avoid extra configuration and instead always use the new dereference behavior. However, I think a good example for why the existing behavior is worth preserving by default is OpenDev\u0027s `opendev-prod-hourly` pipeline. This is an independent pipeline triggered hourly using the timer trigger that potentially needs extra consideration if we can enqueue multiple entries that span an hour. This is unlikely in the current OpenDev setup due to our semaphores and the jobs running in less than 10 minutes at this point, but in the past before our parallel refactoring it may have been a bigger problem.\n\nAll that to say I think I\u0027ve convinced myself making this configurable is a good thing and I\u0027m writing that down for other reviewers to consider as well.",
      "revId": "a9dc6b03c2898c0dd2f9fb27fd78476cc3caa07a",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
